       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change what I said before. The dose is about twice the maximum, and a prescriber needs to verify it, not an administrator. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Ask the treating physician or another licensed prescriber** to enter the order themselves. If they intend a dose above the labeled maximum, they can document their reasoning and have pharmacy review it.\n- **Give me a dose within range,** such as 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 1000 mg twice daily. I'll enter that right away.\n- **Have the prescriber confirm the dose with me in this conversation.** I would still advise a pharmacy check before I enter it."
